   "html_text": "Cameron Buckner (2018; see also Buckner 2023, Ch. 3) has proposed to answer this question for certain types of ANNs using transformational abstraction: an image is repeatedly transformed by mapping it into simpler feature spaces. These spaces are spanned by properties that increasingly suppress irrelevant information contained in nuisance parameters (e.g., the angle from which a chair is observed). In a deep convolutional neural network, one step in this direction is achieved by two consecutive ",
